1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,503
This frog freezes solid every winter, and

2
00:00:02,503 --> 00:00:03,480
its heart stops.

3
00:00:03,940 --> 00:00:05,691
It's the wood frog, the only North

4
00:00:05,691 --> 00:00:07,700
American frog found north of the Arctic

5
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:08,060
Circle.

6
00:00:08,620 --> 00:00:10,724
But in winter, up to two thirds of the

7
00:00:10,724 --> 00:00:12,440
water in its body turns to ice.

8
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:13,500
No heartbeat.

9
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:14,480
No breathing.

10
00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:15,440
No blood flow.

11
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:17,040
But how does it survive?

12
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:19,380
Its liver floods its body with sugar.

13
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:21,887
That sugar works like antifreeze, so ice

14
00:00:21,887 --> 00:00:23,320
can't form inside its cells.

15
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:26,625
But in Alaska, it goes further: frozen for

16
00:00:26,625 --> 00:00:27,620
up to 218 days.

17
00:00:27,620 --> 00:00:30,303
And before winter sets in, it can freeze

18
00:00:30,303 --> 00:00:31,980
and thaw again and again.

19
00:00:32,680 --> 00:00:33,760
Then spring comes.

20
00:00:34,180 --> 00:00:35,700
It thaws out and comes back to life.

21
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:38,280
And it hops off to a pond to breed...

22
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:39,860
like winter never happened.

